- intro
this is a "simple" script that checks for specific .txt files and runs respective game. These games aren’t mine, I found them on abandonware websites.
-disclaimer:
these games aren't mine, I don't own them in any way and I'm sharing them without any intent to make producer lose money nor promote privacy, this is just a glorified school project. (Pls don't sue me)
before this I didn't really know much about MS-DOS so AI helped me with lot of this (pls don't judge)
-	How it works:
The main launch script runs in launcher.bat. On winXP PCs hide.vbs is supposed to be put into startup folder in order to be functioning from the start. The hide.vbs is a small script to hide the checker window (if you want to see it, just open launcher.bat manually). HOWEVER, this makes the PC check floppy drive every 2 seconds, so it is quite hefty on the floppy drive itself.
-	Launcher.bat explanation:
1.	CHECK function:
Basically bunch of if statements that check if there is a file on drive A (floppy drive), to add a new game, you have to specify a txt file (txt file itself can be empty, it’s just the name) and make a function RUN_GAME##
2.	RUN_GAME function:
Just checks into the directory for game EXE and puts it into GAME_EXE variable, also sets FLOPPY_FILE to game txt on floppy
3.	MONITOR_GAME function:
This is where the fun begins, so first, checks every two minutes, then, if it finds the txt (set in the FLOPPY_FILE var) and runs the game set in the GAME_EXE var
4.	The last part (game killer):
If there is no floppy, kills the process trough win task manager

-	How to add a game into this
You get the game, preferably .exe and just add it into launcher.bat. I have good experience with DOSBox and ZDoom, if you prefer any other, be my guest (what can I do about it?)
!!! DOSBox: the "DOSBox 0.74-3 Options.bat" is for some reason for all dosboxes, for automatic mount of EXEs/IMGs you have to edit "dosbox.conf" in each directory of each game
